        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12444895/comment/12797613",
          "id": "12797613",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=angela",
            "name": "angela",
            "key": "anchela",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Angela Schreiber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "i don't agree with the proposed changes. the jackrabbit-webdav project must not have any notion of JCR as\nit is designed to work with any kind of webdav implementation. the constants invented for the JCR remoting over\nwebdav do not belong there from my point of view.\n\n> For now the patch simply copies the relevant code in the shared classes to o.a.j.spi2dav.server\n\nthen i would rather copy the constants to spi2dav.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=angela",
            "name": "angela",
            "key": "anchela",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Angela Schreiber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2010-01-07T13:07:08.499+0000",
          "updated": "2010-01-07T13:07:08.499+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12444895/comment/12797619",
          "id": "12797619",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "> the jackrabbit-webdav project must not have any notion of JCR\n\nWhat about existing classes like o.a.j.webdav.observation.ObservationConstants?\n\nI definitely agree that we don't want to introduce a JCR API dependency on jackrabbit-webdav. But just like we include support for other WebDAV extensions like DASL or the extra properties used by Microsoft, can we not also include similar support for the JCR extensions?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
